From: Daniel Martin <dmanlfc@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: qcom: honour the aspm-no-l0s DT property

Some boards log a flood of correctable AER errors with L0s enabled on a
link that is fine on other boards with the same SoC. Clear L0s from the
root port's link capabilities when the controller node has aspm-no-l0s.

---
diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
index 0ad66c62c..85400dabd 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
@@ -344,7 +344,8 @@ static void qcom_pcie_clear_aspm_l0s(struct dw_pcie *pci)
 	u16 offset;
 	u32 val;
 
-	if (!pcie->cfg->no_l0s)
+	if (!pcie->cfg->no_l0s &&
+	    !of_property_read_bool(pci->dev->of_node, "aspm-no-l0s"))
 		return;
 
 	offset = dw_pcie_find_capability(pci, PCI_CAP_ID_EXP);
